{"format":1,"kind":"pfa","id":"pfa-1961","version":"pfa-1961-25f7714d","year":1961,"season":"1961","label":"NFL (computed)","local":false,"source":{"provider":"Pro Football Archives","edition":"The 1961 NFL season, computed","compiler":"Pro Football Archives (the facts: starts, positions, box scores); the overall ours, computed from them and read off Madden NFL 2002 (maddenratings.net)","url":"https://www.profootballarchives.com/1961nfl.html","retrieved":"2026-11-09","method":"computed","rawScale":"value","conversion":"Ours, computed: no game rated this NFL season. Each player's season value (his club's credit, its points per game against the league's to the power 0.25, offence and defence apart, shared out: the offensive line by starts; quarterbacks, backs, receivers and tight ends by production, rushing and receiving yards, 0.2 a passing yard, 40 a touchdown and less 60 an interception thrown, and by starts; defenders two thirds by starts and one third by plays, 2 a sack where recorded, 1.5 an interception, 1 a fumble recovered, 1 a return touchdown; kickers by field goals, extra points and accuracy against the league) is ranked among the league-season's players at his game position (ties by starts, then games played) and read off Madden NFL 2002's overalls at that position (the 2001 season: maddenratings.net's 31 team spreadsheets, punters left out), as many of each Madden team's best as the season carries per club, by linear interpolation; rounded and held to 1–99. Then each club moves toward its results: its target is T = μ + √r × S ÷ m, where S is its Simple Rating System (its margins by least squares with a home edge, the NFL's ratings summing to nought) from the season's 98 games, r = 0.698 their reliability, m = 1.956 points of margin a game for each point of the strength the match model plays (its lineup's offence and defence, their mean), measured over 160,000 simulated games under the season's rules, and μ = 78.57 the clubs' mean strength before the move